      "text": "To find the ratio of \\( AC \\) to \\( BD \\), we need to determine the lengths of \\( AC \\) and \\( BD \\) first.\n\nGiven:\n- \\( AB = 2 \\) units\n- \\( BC = 5 \\) units\n- \\( AD = 14 \\) units\n\nSince \\( A, B, C, \\) and \\( D \\) are points on a line in that order, we can express the positions of these points as follows:\n- Point \\( A \\) is at position 0.\n- Point \\( B \\) is at position 2.\n- Point \\( C \\) is at position 2 + 5 = 7.\n- Point \\( D \\) is at position 2 + 5 + 14 = 21.\n\nNow, we can calculate the lengths \\( AC \\) and \\( BD \\):\n- \\( AC = C - A = 7 - 0 = 7 \\) units.\n- \\( BD = D - B = 21 - 2 = 19 \\) units.\n\nThe ratio of \\( AC \\) to \\( BD \\) is:\n\\[\n\\frac{AC}{BD} = \\frac{7}{19}\n\\]\n\nThus, the ratio of \\( AC \\) to \\( BD \\) is \\(\\boxed{\\frac{7}{19}}\\).",
