      "text": "To find the ratio of \\(AC\\) to \\(BD\\), we start by determining the lengths of the segments \\(AC\\) and \\(BD\\).\n\nGiven:\n- \\(AB = 2\\) units\n- \\(BC = 5\\) units\n- \\(AD = 14\\) units\n\nFirst, we calculate the length of segment \\(AC\\):\n\\[\nAC = AB + BC = 2 + 5 = 7 \\text{ units}\n\\]\n\nNext, we calculate the length of segment \\(BD\\):\n\\[\nBD = AD - AB = 14 - 2 = 12 \\text{ units}\n\\]\n\nNow, we find the ratio of \\(AC\\) to \\(BD\\):\n\\[\n\\frac{AC}{BD} = \\frac{7}{12}\n\\]\n\nThus, the ratio of \\(AC\\) to \\(BD\\) is \\(\\boxed{\\frac{7}{12}}\\).",
